{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2026-10-26T18:29:03.795127+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-26T18:29:03.893389+00:00", "id": 23673342, "conceptrecid": "23673341", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23673342", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23673341", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23673342", "metadata": {"title": "Fixed-reference Benefit-of-the-Doubt index on Alkire-Foster censored headcounts: replication package", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23673342", "publication_date": "2026-10-26", "description": "<p>Replication package accompanying manuscript version 4 of &ldquo;Pesos end&oacute;genos e refer&ecirc;ncia fixa na mensura&ccedil;&atilde;o territorial da pobreza multidimensional: evid&ecirc;ncia para o Brasil, 1991 a 2022&rdquo;. The method evaluates Alkire-Foster censored deprivation headcounts against a frozen 2010 state-level reference with a proportional coefficient restriction. The archive contains the R implementation, run_all.R, English replication instructions, variable documentation, aggregate results for 2010 and 2022 with a historical extension to 1991 and 2000, robustness results, tests and SHA-256 manifests. Census microdata and household intermediate bases are excluded. The main 2010/2022 scripts obtain official public IBGE inputs; the historical extension requires separately obtained SPSS samples identified in the documentation. Scalar subgroup consistency applies to groups of whole states with fixed population shares, not arbitrary within-state partitions. The v4 review re-estimated aggregate scores and relevant checks, rather than rerunning all raw-data processing. Release 1.0.0 corresponds to manuscript v4 (26 October 2026). The manuscript is unpublished. Code and documentation: MIT license. Repository: https://github.com/moisesluna2026/bod-fixed-mpi</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Brand\u00e3o, Mois\u00e9s Luna", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Mariano, Enzo Barberio", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Rebelatto, Daisy Aparecida do Nasc