version_downloads": 0, "version_unique_downloads": 0, "version_unique_views": 0, "version_views": 0}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-26T14:48:10.008382+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-26T14:48:10.265391+00:00", "id": 23665237, "conceptrecid": "23665236", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23665237", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23665236", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23665237", "metadata": {"title": "Semantic Alpha: replication package for \"Semantic Reliability and Cronbach's Alpha: Pre-testing Psychometric Scales with Large Language Model Embeddings\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23665237", "publication_date": "2026-10-26", "description": "<p>Code, data and cached sentence embeddings that reproduce every table and every reported number in the manuscript \"Semantic Reliability and Cronbach's Alpha: Pre-testing Psychometric Scales with Large Language Model Embeddings\" (submitted to Behavior Research Methods).</p>\n<p>A single Python script computes Semantic Alpha (standardized Cronbach's alpha from cosine similarities of item embeddings), chance-level reference similarities, baseline-adjusted alpha, permutation tests, item loadings and centered kernel alignment for six embedding models. It also computes agreement with the published alphas of 448 IPIP scales, with bootstrap confidence intervals. With the included embedding cache the analysis runs in about a minute without downloading any models; the embeddings can also be recomputed from the pinned model revisions. See README.md for instructions.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Myrland, \u00d8ystein", "affiliation": "UiT The Arctic University of Norway", "orcid": "0000-0002-0284-9062"}], "keywords": ["psychometric scale development, Cronbach's alpha, semantic similarity, sentence embeddings, large language models, reliability, IPIP, SERVQUAL"], "version": "1.0.0", "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}}]}, "res