: 0, "version_unique_views": 1, "version_views": 1}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-26T06:25:25.851995+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-26T06:25:26.055571+00:00", "id": 23637733, "conceptrecid": "23637732", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23637733", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23637732", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23637733", "metadata": {"title": "Replication package for \"Evidence Contracts for Auditing Human\u2013AI Software Development: Interpreting Pull-Request Traces under Generative AI\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23637733", "publication_date": "2026-10-25", "description": "<p>Replication package for the article \"Evidence Contracts for Auditing Human&ndash;AI Software Development: Interpreting Pull-Request Traces under Generative AI\". An evidence contract is an executable specification of the evidence a claim about an AI-assisted pull request requires and of the signals declared insufficient for it; an interpreter returns, claim by claim, one of four verdicts (supported, not applicable, unresolved, contradicted) with a diagnosis.</p>\n<p>The package contains the contract interpreter and its tests (including exhaustive checks of four properties of the verdict semantics), every clause with its bindings, the pseudonymized snapshots of the public pull-request records used in the study (accounts replaced by truncated SHA-256 hashes, bots flagged, no comment text), the manual and AI codes of the coded samples, the scripts of the additional checks and of the stress test, and every result file used for the results reported in the article. Retrieval scripts use the GitHub CLI and need network access; the snapshots are shipped so that this step can be skipped.</p>\n<p>How to reproduce: see README.md and replication/README.md. Install the packages in replication/requirements-lock.txt (Python 3.14), run `python3 -m pytest simulation/ -q` (40 tests) and the commands listed in replication/README.md; `shasum -a 256 -c replication/SHA256SUMS` verifies every file.</p>\n<p>Not included: the coding sheets with approvers' account names, the case files with public comment text used by the AI coders, and the code of the allocation prototype from an earlier audit (its frozen outputs are kept only for the interpreter's tests). Code is released under the MIT licence; data and results under CC BY 4.0.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Pelechano, Vicente", "affiliation": "Universitat Polit\u00e8cnica de Val\u00e8ncia", "orcid": "0000-0003-1090-230X"}, {"name": "Mestre Gascon, Antoni", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0000-0001-8572-2579"}, {"name": "Albert Albiol, Manuela", "affiliation": "Universitat Polit\u00e8cnica de Val\u00e8ncia", "orcid": "0000-0003-3747-400X"}, {"name": "Gil, Miriam", "affiliation": "Universitat de Val\u00e8ncia", "orcid": "0000-0002-2987-1825"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23637732"}}]}, "notes": "<p>Supports the manuscript submitted to Information and Software Technology. The two AI coders of the held-out sample are separate instances of one model; the held-out check is not a human validation.</p>"}, "title": "Replication package for \"Evidence Contracts for Auditing Human\u2013AI Software Development: Interpreting Pull-Request Traces under Generative AI\"", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23637733", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23637733?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23637733", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23637733", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23637733", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637732", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23637732", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23637732", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23637732", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23637733/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23637733/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23637733/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-26T06:25:26.055571+00:00", "recid": "23637733", "revision": 4, "files": [{"id": "af04b045-754f-4af7-89b0-36001e8330de", "key": "replication_package.zip", "size": 1184480, "checksum": "md5:ed8a12a4c567fef963cca925418ea5e5", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23637733/files/replication_package.zip/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "1661040"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 0, "unique_downloads": 0, "views": 5, "unique_views": 4, "version_downloads": 0, "version_unique_downloads": 0, "version_unique_views": 4, "version_views": 5}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-26T05:37:47.568648+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-26T05:37:47.723917+00:00", "id": 23656859, "conceptrecid": "23656858", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23656859", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23656858", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23656859", "metadata": {"title": "Replication package for \"Measuring What Learned Compiler Optimization Really Gains\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23656859", "publication_date": "2026-10-26", "description": "<p>Replication package for the paper \"Measuring What Learned Compiler Optimization Really Gains\", under double-anonymous review.</p>\n<p>It contains the data, code and results behind every table, figure and number in the paper: the LORE timings, hardware counters and loop metadata as extracted from the original database; the static features and pretrained embeddings of every loop; the repaired corpus, the family assignment of every loop and the 20 carves of each split; the per-loop predictions and per-carve results of every model; the code that repairs, groups and splits the corpus and trains and scores the models; the reimplementation of LoopLearner with the predictions of its 180 runs; and the checks on versions 2 and 3 of LOOPerSet. README.md maps each result to its files and gives the commands to recompute or retrain it.</p>\n<p>LORE's loop bodies are not included: the original database is no longer hosted by its authors and its license could not be determined. LOOPerSet is distributed by its authors.</p>\n<p>Code is under the MIT license, and the data and results derived by the authors under CC BY 4.0. Measurements taken from LORE remain subject to its terms.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Anonymous", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["compiler optimization", "machine learning", "loop transformations", "data leakage", "code duplication", "evaluation methodology"], "related_identifiers": [{"